## T-172 — every archived path is tracked at the archived tag — FAILS

$ tar tzf noye-project-v0.28.0.tar.gz | sed 's#^\./##;s#/$##' | sort -u > archive-paths.txt
$ git ls-tree -r --name-only 0.28.0 | sort -u > tracked-paths.txt
$ comm -23 archive-paths.txt tracked-paths.txt | wc -l
97

97 archived paths are not tracked at tag 0.28.0. FAILS.

## T-173 — byte-identical when built twice — NOT MEANINGFULLY TESTABLE pre-fix

Not run: T-171/T-172 already establish the archive is not tag-derived,
so reproducibility from the tag is moot until the fix lands. (Run
post-fix instead — see subject-03d-tests.log.)

## T-174 — refuses to build from a dirty or untagged tree — FAILS

$ touch UNTRACKED_DIRTY_TEST_FILE.txt
$ ./package.sh /tmp/.../dirty-test
Packaging Noye v0.28.0
  archive: .../noye-project-v0.28.0.tar.gz
  readme:  .../noye-README-v0.28.0.md
Done.
$ echo "exit code: $?"
exit code: 0

Built successfully against a dirty working tree with no warning and no
non-zero exit. FAILS — the script has no concept of "dirty" or
"untagged" at all.

## T-175 — flat unpack, filename carries version — PASSES (guard, subject 03a's fix)

$ tar tzf noye-project-v0.28.0.tar.gz | head -3
./
./README.md
./docs/

Flat, no `noye-0.28.0/` parent. Filename `noye-project-v0.28.0.tar.gz`.
Unaffected by this defect — recorded to confirm the fix does not
regress it.

## T-176 — Cargo.lock is present — FAILS

$ tar tzf noye-project-v0.28.0.tar.gz | grep -x './Cargo.lock'
(no output — ABSENT)

`package.sh:32`'s `--exclude='Cargo.lock'` excludes it, per the
pre-DEC-019 rule this subject reverses. FAILS.

## T-177 — pushing a tag produces a GitHub Release with the archive attached — FAILS (does not exist)

$ ls .github/workflows/
ci.yml

$ gh release view 0.28.0
release not found

No release workflow exists. Tag `0.28.0` was pushed 2026-07-29 as a
tag-only release (ROADMAP.md) with nothing attached — this is the
condition subject 03d exists to fix, not a run to compare against.

## Summary

Five must-fail-first tests (T-171, T-172, T-174, T-176, T-177) FAIL as
expected against the pre-fix tree. T-173 deferred to post-fix (moot
pre-fix). T-175 already passes and is carried as a guard.
